---
title: Kitchen sink
description: Every construct markdown() renders, in one page, for checking Prose's type, spacing, and themes.
---

<script>
  import { Button, ComboBox, InlineLoading, Stack, Tag } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import Add from "carbon-icons-svelte/lib/Add.svelte";

  let count = 0;

  const regions = [
    { id: "us-south", text: "Dallas" },
    { id: "eu-de", text: "Frankfurt" },
    { id: "jp-tok", text: "Tokyo", disabled: true },
  ];

  let selectedId = "us-south";
  let status = "";

  $: selected = regions.find((region) => region.id === selectedId);

  function filterRegions(item, value) {
    return item.text.toLowerCase().includes(value.toLowerCase());
  }

  function handleSelect(event) {
    status = `Deploying to ${event.detail.selectedItem.text}`;
  }
</script>

## Running copy

Prose sets body copy at a comfortable measure. This paragraph is long enough to wrap several times, so you can judge line length, line height, and the space between paragraphs. It mixes *emphasis*, **strong text**, ***both at once***, ~~strikethrough~~, and `inline code` in the middle of a sentence.

A second paragraph follows, with links of every kind: an [inline link](https://carbondesignsystem.com "Carbon Design System"), a [reference link][carbon], a [collapsed reference][], an autolink <https://svelte.dev>, and a link wrapping code: [`TableOfContents`](#tables). Press <DocKbd label="Ctrl" /> + <DocKbd label="K" /> to search, or <DocKbd label="Escape" /> to close.

Inline code next to punctuation: (`value`), "`key`", `a`/`b`, and `selectedIds`. Braces stay literal: `{ id, text }` in code and { id, text } in prose. Escapes: \*not emphasis\*, \`not code\`, and a literal \\ backslash.

Bare URLs link themselves: https://carbondesignsystem.com and www.svelte.dev, and so do emails like team@example.com, but a version like carbon-components-svelte@0.113.1 stays text. Footnotes collect at the end of the page.[^prose] A second reference reuses its number.[^prose] Another note.[^svelte]

[^prose]: Prose styles the plain HTML that `markdown()` renders.
[^svelte]: Svelte markup passes through as written.

A line with a hard break at the end  
continues on the next line, and this one has a backslash break\
too.

[carbon]: https://carbondesignsystem.com
[collapsed reference]: https://github.com/carbon-design-system/carbon-components-svelte

## Keyboard keys

Keys sit inside running copy without pushing lines apart. Open the command palette with <DocKbd label="Ctrl" /> + <DocKbd label="Shift" /> + <DocKbd label="P" />, type to filter, then use <DocKbd label="ArrowDown" /> and <DocKbd label="ArrowUp" /> to move through the results. <DocKbd label="Enter" /> runs the highlighted command and <DocKbd label="Escape" /> closes the palette. On a Mac, use <DocKbd label="Cmd" /> instead of <DocKbd label="Ctrl" />, and <DocKbd label="Option" /> instead of <DocKbd label="Alt" />.

The same paragraph without keys, for comparing line spacing: open the command palette with Ctrl + Shift + P, type to filter, then use ArrowDown and ArrowUp to move through the results. Enter runs the highlighted command and Escape closes the palette. On a Mac, use Cmd instead of Ctrl, and Option instead of Alt.

