## Lists

An unordered list, tight:

- Create a project
- Generate an API key
  - Scope it to one environment
  - Rotate it every 90 days
- Install the CLI

An ordered list that starts at 3, loose:

3. Scale `replicas` to `0`.

4. Delete the service. This item is long enough to wrap, so you can see how a wrapped line aligns with the text above it rather than the marker.

5. Revoke the API key.

A task list:

- [x] Write the guide
- [x] Add the examples
- [ ] Review with the team
- [ ] Publish

Mixed nesting:

1. Configure the service
   - `name`, required
   - `region`, defaults to `us-south`
2. Deploy it

   ```sh
   acme deploy --project my-app
   ```

3. Verify the deployment

## Quotes and alerts

> A plain blockquote. Use it for quotations, not for notices.
>
> It can span paragraphs, and hold `code` and **emphasis**.
>
> > A nested quote.

> [!NOTE]
> Keys are scoped to one project.

> [!TIP]
> Use one key per environment, so revoking one doesn't break the others.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Regions can't be changed after you create a project.

> [!WARNING]
> Requests over the limit return `429`. Retry with backoff.

> [!CAUTION]
> Revoking a key breaks every client that uses it.
>
> This alert has a second paragraph.

## Tables

| Setting | Type | Default | Notes |
| :-- | :-- | :-: | --: |
| `name` | `string` | — | **Required** |
| `region` | `"us-south" \| "eu-de"` | `"us-south"` | Closest to most users |
| `replicas` | `number` | `2` | Scale with traffic |
| `labels` | `Record<string, string>` | `{}` | Shown in the [dashboard](#tables) |

A narrow table:

| Key | Action |
| --- | --- |
| <DocKbd label="Enter" /> | Select |
| <DocKbd label="Escape" /> | Close |

## Code

A JavaScript block:

```js
export default {
  port: Number(process.env.PORT ?? 8080),
  env: { LOG_LEVEL: process.env.LOG_LEVEL ?? "info" },
};
```

A Svelte block with a long line, to check horizontal scrolling:

```svelte
<script>
  import { Button } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

<Button kind="primary" size="field" icon={Add} iconDescription="Add a new item to the list" on:click={() => (open = true)}>Add item</Button>
```

A shell block:

```sh
bun add -d carbon-preprocess-svelte
```

## Code features

Fence metadata and inline markers, in the syntaxes Docusaurus, VitePress, and Expressive Code use.

Highlighted lines and a file name: `title="…" {6-9,16}`.

```svelte title="RegionPicker.svelte" {6-9,16}
<script>
  import { ComboBox } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  export let regions = [];

  /** Match anywhere in the name, ignoring case. */
  function shouldFilterItem(item, value) {
    return item.text.toLowerCase().includes(value.toLowerCase());
  }
</script>

<ComboBox
  labelText="Region"
  placeholder="Select a region"
  items={regions}
  {shouldFilterItem}
/>
```

A change, marked with `// [!code ++]` and `// [!code --]` at line ends:

```js title="svelte.config.js"
import { vitePreprocess } from "@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte";
import { optimizeImports } from "carbon-preprocess-svelte"; // [!code --]
import { markdown, optimizeImports } from "carbon-preprocess-svelte"; // [!code ++]

export default {
  extensions: [".svelte", ".md"], // [!code ++]
  preprocess: [vitePreprocess(), optimizeImports()], // [!code --]
  preprocess: [markdown(), vitePreprocess(), optimizeImports()], // [!code ++]
};
```

Focus on the lines that matter; the rest recede until you point at the block: `focus={14-18}`.

```svelte focus={14-18}
<script>
  import {
    DataTable,
    Toolbar,
    ToolbarContent,
    ToolbarSearch,
  } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  export let headers = [];
  export let rows = [];
</script>

<DataTable {headers} {rows}>
  <Toolbar>
    <ToolbarContent>
      <ToolbarSearch persistent shouldFilterRows />
    </ToolbarContent>
  </Toolbar>
</DataTable>
```

Line numbers, starting where an excerpt starts: `showLineNumbers=12`. Marks still count from the block's first line: `{3-6}`. Click a number to copy a link to the line; shift-click another for a range.

```js showLineNumbers=12 {3-6}
export function formatBytes(bytes) {
  const units = ["B", "KB", "MB", "GB"];
  const exponent = Math.min(
    Math.floor(Math.log(bytes) / Math.log(1024)),
    units.length - 1,
  );
  const value = bytes / 1024 ** exponent;
  return `${value.toFixed(1)} ${units[exponent]}`;
}
```

A terminal session: `$ ` lines are commands, the rest is output. Copy takes the commands only, and each command has its own copy button on hover.

```sh
$ bun add -d carbon-preprocess-svelte
bun add v1.3.0

installed carbon-preprocess-svelte@0.11.49

1 package installed [412.00ms]
$ bun run dev

  VITE v7.1.0  ready in 386 ms

  ➜  Local:   http://localhost:5173/
```

A command continued with `\` copies as one command:

```sh
$ npx sv create my-app \
    --template minimal \
    --types ts
$ cd my-app
```

npm commands come in every package manager. The choice applies to every block on the page, and the URL keeps it (`?pm=bun`).

```sh
npm install -D carbon-preprocess-svelte
npm run dev -- --open
```

Files that belong together, as tabs: `::: code-group`, with each file named by `[label]` or `title="…"`.

::: code-group

```svelte [+page.svelte]
<script>
  import RegionPicker from "$lib/RegionPicker.svelte";
  import { regions } from "./regions.js";
</script>

<RegionPicker {regions} />
```

```js [regions.js]
export const regions = [
  { id: "us-south", text: "Dallas" },
  { id: "eu-de", text: "Frankfurt" },
  { id: "jp-tok", text: "Tokyo" },
];
```

```js title="svelte.config.js"
import { markdown, optimizeImports } from "carbon-preprocess-svelte";

export default {
  extensions: [".svelte", ".md"],
  preprocess: [markdown(), optimizeImports()],
};
```

:::

Many files: the tabs scroll sideways, the selected one stays in view, and arrows at the edges show there's more.

::: code-group

